WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.931
Describing People, Places and Problems.

2
00:00:03.211 --> 00:00:06.838
Day 12 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

3
00:00:08.588 --> 00:00:09.612
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.892 --> 00:00:15.332
Today's goal: describe people, places, things and problems clearly, and compare options.

5
00:00:15.612 --> 00:00:21.607
You'll use this to report lost items, explain a bug, choose a hotel, or find a person in a crowd.

6
00:00:22.957 --> 00:00:23.810
Part 1.

7
00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.754
Adjectives: where they go.

8
00:00:27.004 --> 00:00:30.119
a big black suitcase, an old building, a quiet room.

9
00:00:30.399 --> 00:00:31.615
The room is quiet.

10
00:00:31.895 --> 00:00:33.089
The app is slow.

11
00:00:33.369 --> 00:00:34.500
She looks tired.

12
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:45.041
Order (when you use several): opinion, then size, then age, then colour, then material, then noun: a nice small old red leather bag (in practice, use 2 to 3).

13
00:00:46.391 --> 00:00:47.266
Part 2.

14
00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:48.783
Describing people.

15
00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.399
Here is a quick table:

16
00:00:51.679 --> 00:00:52.895
Topic, and Words.

17
00:00:53.175 --> 00:00:56.865
Height and build: tall, short, average height, slim, well-built.

18
00:00:57.145 --> 00:01:00.751
Hair: short or long, straight or curly, black or grey, bald.

19
00:01:01.031 --> 00:01:04.017
Age: young, middle-aged, elderly, in his thirties.

20
00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:08.095
Clothes: wearing a blue shirt, a red saree, glasses, a cap.

21
00:01:08.375 --> 00:01:12.748
Personality: friendly, helpful, quiet, confident, patient, strict.

22
00:01:14.098 --> 00:01:15.037
You could say:

23
00:01:15.317 --> 00:01:18.261
He's about 60, short, with grey hair and glasses.

24
00:01:18.541 --> 00:01:20.055
He's wearing a white kurta.

25
00:01:21.405 --> 00:01:22.301
Part 3.

26
00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:24.267
Describing places and things.

27
00:01:25.517 --> 00:01:31.511
Place: crowded, quiet, clean, noisy, modern, spacious, well-located, far from or close to...

28
00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:37.679
Things: heavy, light, broken, new, second-hand, waterproof, made of steel or plastic or cotton.

29
00:01:37.959 --> 00:01:43.271
Location words: next to, opposite, behind, in front of, between, near, on the corner of.

30
00:01:44.621 --> 00:01:45.539
Part 4.

31
00:01:45.819 --> 00:01:46.651
Comparing.

32
00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.266
Here is a quick table:

33
00:01:49.546 --> 00:01:55.071
Short adjectives, and Long adjectives, and Irregular. cheap, then cheaper, then the cheapest.

34
00:01:55.351 --> 00:02:00.045
Long adjectives: expensive, then more expensive, then the most expensive.

35
00:02:00.325 --> 00:02:04.719
Irregular: good, then better, then the best. big, then bigger, then the biggest.

36
00:02:04.999 --> 00:02:07.858
Long adjectives: comfortable, then more comfortable.

37
00:02:08.138 --> 00:02:12.703
Irregular: bad, then worse, then the worst. easy, then easier, then the easiest.

38
00:02:12.983 --> 00:02:16.055
Long adjectives: convenient, then more convenient.

39
00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:18.981
Irregular: far, then farther, then the farthest.

40
00:02:20.331 --> 00:02:22.101
The metro is faster than the bus.

41
00:02:22.381 --> 00:02:23.939
This is the cheapest option.

42
00:02:24.219 --> 00:02:25.904
It's not as big as the other room.

43
00:02:27.254 --> 00:02:28.214
Part 5.

44
00:02:28.494 --> 00:02:30.478
Describing a problem (any kind).

45
00:02:31.728 --> 00:02:33.093
Here is a quick table:

46
00:02:33.373 --> 00:02:35.165
Situation, and Description.

47
00:02:35.445 --> 00:02:36.448
Lost bag:

48
00:02:36.728 --> 00:02:39.949
It's a medium-sized black backpack with a red keychain.

49
00:02:40.229 --> 00:02:41.893
It has my laptop inside.

50
00:02:42.173 --> 00:02:43.261
Broken appliance:

51
00:02:43.541 --> 00:02:46.571
The washing machine makes a loud noise and doesn't drain.

52
00:02:46.851 --> 00:02:48.173
It started yesterday.

53
00:02:48.453 --> 00:02:49.349
App bug:

54
00:02:49.629 --> 00:02:53.128
The app freezes on the payment screen every time I tap 'Pay'.

55
00:02:53.408 --> 00:02:54.773
I've restarted the phone.

56
00:02:55.053 --> 00:02:55.736
Health:

57
00:02:56.016 --> 00:02:58.789
I've had a sharp pain in my lower back for three days.

58
00:02:59.069 --> 00:03:00.392
It's worse in the morning.

59
00:03:01.742 --> 00:03:10.937
Useful problem words: broken, not working, stuck, leaking, cracked, missing, damaged, too loud, too slow, freezing, overheating, keeps (+ -ing):

60
00:03:11.217 --> 00:03:12.390
It keeps crashing.

61
00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:14.679
Part 6.

62
00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:17.860
Conversation: lost bag at the metro station.

63
00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.137
Here is how the conversation goes.

64
00:03:21.417 --> 00:03:24.873
Excuse me, I think I left my bag on the train.

65
00:03:25.153 --> 00:03:26.731
Which train, and what time?

66
00:03:27.011 --> 00:03:31.790
The one that arrived at platform 2 at about 9:15, from Whitefield.

67
00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.606
Can you describe the bag?

68
00:03:33.886 --> 00:03:36.254
It's a medium-sized black backpack.

69
00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:39.777
It's quite heavy, and it has a red keychain on the zip.

70
00:03:41.127 --> 00:03:42.727
The conversation continues.

71
00:03:43.007 --> 00:03:44.223
What's inside?

72
00:03:44.503 --> 00:03:47.831
My laptop, a charger, and a blue water bottle.

73
00:03:48.111 --> 00:03:51.097
My office ID card is in the front pocket.

74
00:03:51.377 --> 00:03:52.487
Okay.

75
00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.260
Please fill in this form.

76
00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.268
We'll check with the last station.

77
00:03:56.548 --> 00:03:57.487
Thank you.

78
00:03:57.767 --> 00:03:59.751
How long does it usually take?

79
00:04:00.031 --> 00:04:01.140
About an hour.

80
00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.745
Please wait near the customer care counter.

81
00:04:05.095 --> 00:04:06.695
The conversation continues.

82
00:04:06.975 --> 00:04:07.914
Okay.

83
00:04:08.194 --> 00:04:11.138
Here's my phone number, in case you find it.

84
00:04:12.488 --> 00:04:13.427
Part 7.

85
00:04:13.707 --> 00:04:14.624
Practice.

86
00:04:15.874 --> 00:04:16.514
1.

87
00:04:16.794 --> 00:04:19.994
Compare: cab versus metro (fast, cheap, comfortable).

88
00:04:21.344 --> 00:04:22.261
Success:

89
00:04:22.541 --> 00:04:23.629
Sample answer.

90
00:04:23.909 --> 00:04:29.115
The metro is cheaper and faster than a cab during rush hour, but a cab is more comfortable.

91
00:04:30.465 --> 00:04:31.169
2.

92
00:04:31.449 --> 00:04:36.249
Describe a person you can see right now in 3 sentences (height, hair, clothes).

93
00:04:36.529 --> 00:04:37.275
3.

94
00:04:37.555 --> 00:04:44.019
Describe a problem with something at home using: what's wrong, then since when, then how bad, then what you tried.

95
00:04:45.369 --> 00:04:46.287
Success:

96
00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:47.655
Sample answer.

97
00:04:47.935 --> 00:04:49.471
The kitchen tap is leaking.

98
00:04:49.751 --> 00:04:51.244
It started two days ago.

99
00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:54.319
It drips all the time, and there's water on the floor.

100
00:04:54.599 --> 00:04:56.327
I tightened it, but it didn't help.

101
00:04:57.677 --> 00:04:58.551
Part 8.

102
00:04:58.831 --> 00:04:59.877
Speak today.

103
00:05:01.127 --> 00:05:04.647
Describe your home or office to someone in 5 sentences.

104
00:05:04.927 --> 00:05:07.999
Compare two options using -er than or more... than.

105
00:05:08.279 --> 00:05:12.204
Describe one problem clearly (at home, at work, or with an app).

106
00:05:13.554 --> 00:05:15.090
That's the end of this lesson.

107
00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:20.042
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

108
00:05:20.322 --> 00:05:26.423
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

